### ====================================================================
### Day 10 Exercise 5 - Backend Milestone Review - Test Evidence
### Support Desk Ticket API
### ====================================================================
### Run the app first:  mvn spring-boot:run
### App starts on port 8080 (see application.properties).
### MongoDB must be running on localhost:27017.
###
### How to use this file:
###   1. Run the Register request (checklist #10) to create a test user.
###   2. Run the Login request (checklist #11) and copy the "token" value.
###   3. Paste the token into the @token variable below.
###   4. Run every request in order to collect evidence for all checklist items.
### ====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 1: Project runs successfully
### The health endpoint proves the Spring Boot application started.
### Expect: 200 OK
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 2: MongoDB connection works
### The login below queries the seeded admin user from MongoDB.
### If MongoDB were down, this would return 500 / connection error.
### Seeded admin credentials: admin@example.com / Admin@12345
### Expect: 200 OK with a JWT token in the response body
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@12345"
}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 10: Register endpoint works
### Creates a brand-new user account and returns a JWT.
### Expect: 201 Created with token, role USER
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Milestone Reviewer",
  "email": "reviewer@example.com",
  "password": "Review@12345"
}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 11: Login endpoint returns JWT
### Login with the registered user to receive a fresh JWT.
### Copy the "token" value from the response and paste it into
### the @token variable at the top of this file.
### Expect: 200 OK with token, tokenType "Bearer", role "USER"
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "reviewer@example.com",
  "password": "Review@12345"
}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 12: Protected endpoints reject missing token
### Calling /api/tickets WITHOUT an Authorization header.
### Expect: 401 Unauthorized
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 13: Protected endpoints accept valid token
### Calling /api/tickets WITH a valid Bearer token.
### Expect: 200 OK with a JSON array of tickets
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 5: Basic CRUD endpoints work - List all tickets
### Expect: 200 OK with JSON array (seeded data proves MongoDB)
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 5: Basic CRUD endpoints work - Get ticket by ID
### Replace TICKET_ID_HERE with a real id from the list above.
### Expect: 200 OK with a single ticket object
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/TICKET_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 5: Basic CRUD endpoints work - Create ticket
### Expect: 201 Created with the new ticket (status defaults to OPEN)
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Milestone review test ticket",
  "description": "Created during the Day 10 backend milestone review.",
  "category": "Bug",
  "priority": "Medium",
  "createdBy": "reviewer@example.com"
}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 6: Filtering works - Filter by status
### Expect: 200 OK, only tickets with status OPEN
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?status=OPEN
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 6: Filtering works - Filter by priority
### Expect: 200 OK, only tickets with priority HIGH
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?priority=HIGH
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 6: Filtering works - Filter by category
### Expect: 200 OK, only tickets with category Email
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?category=Email
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 7: Pagination works
### Page 0, size 3 returns the first 3 tickets.
### Expect: 200 OK with page metadata (totalElements, totalPages, ...)
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 8: Sorting works - Ascending by title
### Expect: 200 OK, tickets ordered alphabetically by title (A -> Z)
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=10&sortBy=title&direction=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 8: Sorting works - Descending by createdAt
### Expect: 200 OK, newest tickets first
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=10&sortBy=createdAt&direction=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 9: Validation errors return clear responses
### Sending a ticket with missing required fields (title, description).
### Expect: 400 Bad Request with a JSON error body listing field errors
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "category": "Bug",
  "priority": "Medium",
  "createdBy": "reviewer@example.com"
}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 9: Duplicate errors return clear responses
### Registering the same email twice triggers a 409 / 400 conflict.
### Expect: 400 / 409 with a clear "Email already exists" message
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Milestone Reviewer",
  "email": "reviewer@example.com",
  "password": "Review@12345"
}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 14: Versioned /api/v1 routes exist - List (v1)
### Expect: 200 OK with JSON array of tickets
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 14: Versioned /api/v1 routes exist - Get by ID (v1)
### Replace TICKET_ID_HERE with a real id.
### Expect: 200 OK with a single ticket object
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets/TICKET_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 14: Versioned /api/v1 routes exist - Create (v1)
### Expect: 201 Created with the new ticket
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "V1 milestone review ticket",
  "description": "Created through the versioned v1 endpoint.",
  "category": "Feature Request",
  "priority": "Low",
  "createdBy": "reviewer@example.com"
}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 15: Report endpoint works - Tickets by status
### Returns a grouped count of tickets by status.
### Expect: 200 OK with label/count array (e.g. OPEN, Closed)
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports/tickets-by-status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 15: Report endpoint works - Tickets by priority
### Returns a grouped count of tickets by priority.
### Expect: 200 OK with label/count array (e.g. HIGH, Low, Medium)
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports/tickets-by-priority
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 16: API documentation endpoint exists
### Returns a JSON document listing every API endpoint.
### This endpoint is public (no token required).
### Expect: 200 OK with application name, version, and endpoints array
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/docs


### ============================================================
### BONUS: Public API info endpoint (versioned)
### Expect: 200 OK with version, status, and documentation link
### ============================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/info


### ============================================================
### CHECKLIST 3 & 4 (code-level, verified in source):
###   - Ticket model uses @Document(collection = "tickets") and @Id
###       -> src/main/java/com/example/supportdesk/model/Ticket.java
###   - TicketRepository extends MongoRepository<Ticket, String>
###       -> src/main/java/com/example/supportdesk/repository/TicketRepository.java
### ============================================================
